 Each vertex in turn takes the least colour","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"none of its already coloured neighbours has (first fit). Degrees are simple degrees (distinct","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other neighbours, self-loops left out); ties go to the lesser vertex index, except for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".coloredNeighbors","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s12CaseIterableP","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/SH","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/saturationLargestFirst":{"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"saturationLargestFirst","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"DSatur (Brélaz 1979): first a vertex of greatest degree, then repeatedly the uncoloured","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex with the most distinct colours among its neighbours, ties to the greatest degree in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the whole graph, then to the lesser index. Exact on bipartite graphs. O((n + m) log n).","type":"text"}],"title":"ColoringStrategy.saturationLargestFirst","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/saturationlargestfirst","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/saturationLargestFirst"},"doc://ColoringModule/SQ":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/SQ","title":"Swift.Equatable"},"doc://ColoringModule/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","ty